       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it is about twice the maximum daily dose of metformin.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Extended-release is capped at 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nPlease confirm which of these you intended:\n1. **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), which may be what you meant.\n2. **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily or 567 mg three times daily. Standard tablets come in 500, 850 and 1000 mg, so 500 mg three times daily or 850 mg twice daily are more practical.\n3. **Another dose.** Tell me the dose and frequency.\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. I'd like your confirmation first because of the safety concern."
      }
